-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zeigerer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>McBrayer</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>McGraw</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Insulin stimulation of GLUT4 exocytosis, but not its inhibition of endocytosis, is dependent on RabGAP AS160</article-title>.<source>Mol Biol Cell</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>4406</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>4415</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15254270</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eguez</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Chavez</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Miinea</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kane</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lienhard</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>McGraw</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Full intracellular retention of GLUT4 requires AS160 Rab GTPase activating protein</article-title>.<source>Cell Metab</source><year>2005</year>;<volume>2</volume>:<fpage>263</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16213228</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruss</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Arias</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><name><surname>Lienhard</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Cartee</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Increased phosphorylation of Akt substrate of 160 kDa (AS160) in rat skeletal muscle in response to insulin or contractile activity</article-title>.<source>D